// RS17.
//
// The zoo's RC11-vs-RC17 witness: a release store continued by a same-thread
//   relaxed FADD, and an acquire load of the result that then loads y's old
//   value. RC11's release sequence continues through the relaxed FADD, so the
//   acquire load synchronises with it; C++17's is continued only by
//   read-modify-writes, so it does not.
//
// Asserted below, by source:
//   herd7 on the zoo's cat models, run on this program: SC forbids, TSO
//     forbids, Coherence allows, RC11 forbids, RC17 allows, OD-LSO allows.
//   the zoo's equivalence and ordering edges:
//     VbD forbids. Equivalent to SC (zoo edge).
//     x86-TSO forbids. Equivalent to TSO (zoo edge).
//     ClightTSO forbids. Equivalent to x86-TSO (zoo edge).
//     RC11z forbids. Equivalent to RC11 (zoo edge).
//   Not asserted, for want of a verdict to check against: MRD, CC, PC, PRAM,
//     Causal, Slow, Local, POCausal, RYW, MR, MW, WFR. RA, SRA and WRA are
//     defined on release stores and acquire loads, and this program has other
//     accesses. herd7 verdicts are on the zoo's
//     litmus/strictly-weaker/RC11-vs-RC17/mp-rs-add-est-atomic.litmus. The
//     OD-LSO cat model is cpp11.cat with acyclic(sb | rf) added.
x := 0; y := 0;
{
  y.store(1, rlx);
  x.store(1, rel);
  rpx := &x;
  ra := FADD(normal, rlx, rlx, rpx, 1)
} ||| {
  rb := x.load(acq);
  if (rb = 3) {
    rc := y.load(rlx)
  }
} ||| {
  x.store(2, rlx)
}
%%
allow (@x = 3 && rb = 3 && rc = 0) [Coherence, RC17, OD-LSO]
forbid (@x = 3 && rb = 3 && rc = 0) [SC, VbD, TSO, x86-TSO, ClightTSO, RC11,
                                     RC11z]
